From: Arch POWER
Subject: [PATCH] spa/json: qualify isnormal/isinf/signbit for C++ consumers

spa_json_format_float() is a SPA_API_JSON static inline in a public
header, so every C++ translation unit that includes <spa/utils/json.h>
compiles it. It calls isnormal(), isinf() and signbit() unqualified,
relying on the macros from <math.h>.

In C++ those are not macros: libstdc++ undefines them and declares the
functions in namespace std. GCC 16 no longer also injects them into the
global namespace, so the header fails to compile for every C++ consumer:

  json-core.h:453:13: error: isnormal was not declared in this scope;
                             did you mean std::isnormal?

Observed building openal, openexr and qt6-multimedia against
pipewire 1.6.x with GCC 16.1.1.

Qualify them with function-scoped using-declarations under __cplusplus,
which keeps the C path byte-identical and adds no namespace pollution.
---
--- a/spa/include/spa/utils/json-core.h
+++ b/spa/include/spa/utils/json-core.h
@@ -10,6 +10,9 @@
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <string.h>
 #include <math.h>
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+#include <cmath>
+#endif
 #include <float.h>
 
 #include <spa/utils/defs.h>
@@ -450,6 +453,11 @@
 
 SPA_API_JSON char *spa_json_format_float(char *str, int size, float val)
 {
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+	using std::isnormal;
+	using std::isinf;
+	using std::signbit;
+#endif
 	if (SPA_UNLIKELY(!isnormal(val))) {
 		if (isinf(val))
 			val = signbit(val) ? FLT_MIN : FLT_MAX;
